--TEST--
`Core\Server::traceId` returns the trace id of the `traceparent` the request carried, as 32 lower-case hex characters, and every call returns the same id — `rule:observability/an-inbound-traceparent-is-continued`
--HEADERS--
traceparent: 00-4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The header names a trace this request continues, so the id is the header's
// own and not one the server drew. A request that sent none still has an id
// (`rule:observability/a-trace-id-exists-for-every-request`); its value is
// random, so this case pins the continued one.
string $id = Core\Server::traceId();
echo $id, "\n";
echo Core\Str::length($id), "\n";

// One request has one id: a second reading is the same string.
if (Core\Server::traceId() == $id) {
    echo "same id\n";
} else {
    echo "a second id\n";
}
--EXPECT--
4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736
32
same id
